{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <functional>\nusing namespace std;\nusing i64 = long long;\n\nconstexpr i64 MOD = 1000000007;\n\ni64 power(i64 base, i64 exp, i64 mod) {\n    i64 result = 1;\n    base %= mod;\n    while (exp) {\n        if (exp & 1) result = (result * base) % mod;\n        base = (base * base) % mod;\n        exp >>= 1;\n    }\n    return result;\n}\n\nstruct DSU {\n    vector<int> p, r;\n    DSU(int n) : p(n), r(n, 1) {\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) p[i] = i;\n    }\n    int find(int x) {\n        return p[x] == x ? x : p[x] = find(p[x]);\n    }\n    void merge(int x, int y) {\n        x = find(x), y = find(y);\n        if (x == y) return;\n        if (r[x] < r[y]) swap(x, y);\n        p[y] = x;\n        r[x] += r[y];\n    }\n};\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    \n    int n, k;\n    cin >> n >> k;\n    \n    if (k == 0) {\n        cout << power(n, n - 1, MOD) << '\\n';\n        return 0;\n    }\n    \n    DSU dsu(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        dsu.merge(i, (1LL * i * k) % n);\n    }\n    \n    i64 result = 1;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        if (dsu.find(i) != i) continue;\n        i64 comp_size = dsu.r[i];\n        i64 val = power(k, comp_size, n);\n        if (val == 1) {\n            result = (result * n) % MOD;\n        }\n    }\n    \n    cout << result << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\ndef power(base, exp, mod):\n    result = 1\n    base %= mod\n    while exp:\n        if exp & 1:\n            result = (result * base) % mod\n        base = (base * base) % mod\n        exp >>= 1\n    return result\n\nclass DSU:\n    def __init__(self, n):\n        self.p = list(range(n))\n        self.r = [1] * n\n    \n    def find(self, x):\n        if self.p[x] == x:\n            return x\n        self.p[x] = self.find(self.p[x])\n        return self.p[x]\n    \n    def merge(self, x, y):\n        x = self.find(x)\n        y = self.find(y)\n        if x == y:\n            return\n        if self.r[x] < self.r[y]:\n            x, y = y, x\n        self.p[y] = x\n        self.r[x] += self.r[y]\n\ndef main():\n    import sys\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    n = int(data[0])\n    k = int(data[1])\n    \n    MOD = 1000000007\n    \n    if k == 0:\n        print(power(n, n - 1, MOD))\n        return\n    \n    dsu = DSU(n)\n    for i in range(n):\n        dsu.merge(i, (i * k) % n)\n    \n    result = 1\n    for i in range(n):\n        if dsu.find(i) != i:\n            continue\n        comp_size = dsu.r[i]\n        val = power(k, comp_size, n)\n        if val == 1:\n            result = (result * n) % MOD\n    \n    print(result)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.0001147919538198039, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.31319862604141235, -0.08113440126180649, -3.